  "falsifiable_next_experiment": {
    "baseline": "Restart from exact 200-step checkpoint; seed and trainable scope fixed; train/infer tile size 896; current alternating coverage and masked BCE+Dice.",
    "test": "Use fit-only training and the existing real development split (never public validation) with identical native 896 inference and report precision/recall at matched recall plus per-document IoU; repeat fixed seeds. A meaningful result is a reproducible precision gain at matched recall without a material per-document IoU regression. Add a sampler/loss unit test proving pairs share query IDs, negative centers are selected only from known negatives, and query/context/unknown pixels receive zero gradient.",
    "variant": "Same initialization, queries, and update budget; pair a positive-centered and a negative-centered crop for the same eligible query when both exist; normalize each crop loss separately before averaging so one large reviewed tile does not dominate; retain unknown masking. Test an FP-heavier Tversky term only as a separate ablation, not bundled with pairing. Positive-only queries remain positive-only and must not be relabeled as negative."
  },
